{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_pydantic_adapter_pattern", "label": "Pydantic Adapter Pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replace Adapter.set() dict-mutation with Pydantic input models one adapter at a time, starting with ContainerDefinitionAdapter, because hand-rolled rename/default/coercion had no schema validation. Incremental rollout de-risks ServiceAdapter. Pydantic is confined to validating/reshaping deployfish.yml input; boto3 key casing stays plain adapter code. Dual-purpose alias/serialization models, pushing Pydantic into Model.__init__, converting all 8 adapters at once, and letting ValidationError reach the CLI were rejected."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_containerdefinitioninput", "label": "ContainerDefinitionInput", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Validates only the container yaml stanza (ports, ulimits, env/labels shapes). Caller-injected secrets, extra_environment, readonly_root_filesystem, and task_definition_data stay constructor args. labels uses Field(alias=dockerLabels) so the documented key is accepted."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_adapter_convert_contract", "label": "Adapter.convert Contract", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "convert() still returns (data, kwargs) with data shaped like a boto3 describe_* response for Model.__init__; the from-AWS vs from-yaml lazy-loading split is unchanged."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_schemaexception_translation", "label": "SchemaException Translation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "pydantic.ValidationError is caught at the adapter boundary and re-raised as Adapter.SchemaException so handle_model_exceptions can print a terse CLI error instead of Pydantic's multi-line dump."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_config_schema_module", "label": "deployfish.config.schema", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Input models live under config/schema (one file per resource) so they can later compose into a whole-file deployfish.yml validator; adapters consume them and do not own them."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_partial_overlay_model", "label": "ContainerDefinitionOverlayInput", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Derived via create_model/partial_model from the strict input so partial=True overlay containers (ServiceHelperTask) share one field-definition source of truth."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_eager_validation", "label": "Eager Validation at Construction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "model_validate() runs once at adapter construction. Lazy per-get_* validation was rejected because it defeats catching bad input up front. extra=forbid, omitting empty collections, and stricter type coercion are documented intentional behavior changes."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_golden_master_test", "label": "Container Adapter Golden Master", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A corpus through current convert() defends identical output dict shape because the rewrite changes validation mechanism, not the load-bearing contract."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_containerdefinitionadapter", "label": "ContainerDefinitionAdapter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_serviceadapter", "label": "ServiceAdapter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Highest-degree node in the adapters module; converting all adapters in one pass was rejected because it would touch this 60-degree god node without a proven pattern."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_pydantic_adapter_pattern", "target": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_containerdefinitionadapter", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_containerdefinitionadapter", "target": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_containerdefinitioninput", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_containerdefinitionadapter", "target": "docs_adr_0001_pydantic_adapters_adapter_convert_contract", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-pydantic-adapters.md", "source_location": 